CRITERIA (verbatim from the review protocol; EC6 full-text and EC7 retraction are not applied by you)
## Inclusion criteria (all must hold)
| Code | Criterion |
|---|---|
| IC1 | Published 2020–2026 |
| IC2 | Peer-reviewed journal article or conference paper, in English. Any length. Surveys and reviews count |
| IC3 | The system (or, for a survey, the systems surveyed) is **LLM / foundation-model based and agentic or autonomous**: an agent loop, tool use, multi-step planning, memory, multi-agent coordination, or acting on the environment. Conceptual frameworks without an evaluation also count |
| IC4 | Addresses at least one in-scope task: intrusion/anomaly detection · alert triage · threat hunting / attack investigation · CTI extraction/enrichment · IR planning / playbooks · autonomous remediation (incl. RL+LLM hybrids) · forensics / post-incident reporting · offensive / pentest agents |

## Exclusion criteria (any one excludes)
| Code | Criterion |
|---|---|
| EC1 | No LLM / foundation-model component (e.g. RL-only or classical multi-agent systems) |
| EC2 | The LLM is used only as a classifier, detector or text generator, with no agentic behaviour (see IC3) |
| EC3 | The primary topic is the security **of** LLMs/agents themselves (prompt injection, jailbreaks, attacks on agents) |
| EC4 | Not a cybersecurity-operations task (another domain, or "anomaly detection" outside security) |
| EC5 | Not peer-reviewed or not a paper: preprint, thesis, editorial, front matter, proceedings-volume record; or not in English |



